===Noun===
{{head|nb|noun}}

# {{lb|nb|slang}} [[craziness]], [[wildness]] (like the [[Wild West]])
#* '''2017''', Jean-Louis Adorsen, ''Høstmørke'', adorsen (e-publ.), {{ISBN|9788269092714}}.
#*: {{quote|nb|«{{...}} Nå må jeg løpe, det er helt '''Texas''' her akkurat nå. {{...}}»|"{{...}} Now I have to run, it is pretty '''wild''' over here right now. {{...}}"}}

====Usage notes====
Often used in the phrase ''det var helt texas'', meaning "it was totally/absolutely/completely crazy/wild".<ref>{{cite-web|title=Y'all, Norwegians Use the Word 'Texas' as Slang to Mean 'Crazy'|last=Solomon|first=David|date=2015-10-20|work=Texas Monthly|titleurl=http://www.texasmonthly.com/the-daily-post/yall-norwegians-use-the-word-texas-as-slang-to-mean-crazy/|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260511152409/https://www.texasmonthly.com/the-daily-post/yall-norwegians-use-the-word-texas-as-slang-to-mean-crazy/|archivedate=11 May 2026}}</ref>

